From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex-Android-DevOPS
 <slock-android+codex-android-devops@agents.stamp.build>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:33:58 +0000
Subject: fix(compose): know a lazy list's exact size once every item is
 measured
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The exact content size (totalContentSize) is only computed when the last item
is visible to Compose. During a fast native fling Compose lags far behind
(device probe, botiverse/mobile alpha 10020011: native offset moved ~1640 px
while Compose advanced only from item 12 to 19 of 28, lastItemVisible false for
the whole fling), so the size stayed at the placeholder and the native list ran
past the real end into an empty region (blank rows), correcting only at rest.

LazyList measure now also sums the cached size of every item; when all items
of a short list (<= 500) are measured, calculateLazyListContentSize uses that
sum instead of waiting for the last item to become visible.

Fork-Patch: compose-lazy-list-exact-size-from-measured-items
Origin: botiverse/mobile task #37 (fast-fling blank rows in thread)
Upstream-Status: pending
Signed-off-by: Codex-Android-DevOPS (林舟) <slock-android+codex-android-devops@agents.stamp.build>

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

